{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered during the Step 7 sibling sweep of 35ab-f0e0-3e4a-4b72 (fightable-nirvanic-kitten).\n\n## Site\n`ExpressionError(WorkflowError)` is defined at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:251` and raised from workflow execute-time expression resolution (`interpreter.py` and `executor.py`) for wiring/state faults: input not set, no such step output, loop/map var out of scope, missing secret/env, or unresolvable `${{ }}` expression.\n\n## Symptom\n`error_code_for(ExpressionError(...))` currently reaches the broad `LLMError`/`WorkflowError` branch and returns `llm_unavailable`. That asserts a provider outage for a caller/state wiring fault and encourages retries that will not self-heal.\n\n## Operator decision\nLatest DECISION NEEDED comment (operator-approved 2026-09-01) supersedes the earlier `expression_unresolved` option for this ticket: reclassify `ExpressionError -> invalid_input`, matching prior bug 35ab (executor unknown-step -> invalid_input) and dbca (parse/lint -> invalid_input). Give `ExpressionError` an explicit `error_code = \"invalid_input\"` so the mapping is honest regardless of branch order. Preserve dbca AC3 by ensuring genuine execute-time LLM outages still map to `llm_unavailable` through the true outage type/wrapper path. Implement this with ce6b's umbrella narrowing as one coherent change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `ExpressionError` has an explicit `error_code = \"invalid_input\"` and `error_code_for(ExpressionError(...))` returns `invalid_input`, verified by a focused unit/contract test.\n- [ ] A real workflow execute-surface expression-resolution failure returns `invalid_input`, not `llm_unavailable`, verified through the real workflow execution surface or the smallest existing production error conversion seam that exercises the same exception.\n- [ ] A genuine LLM outage inside an execute step still returns `llm_unavailable`, verified by a focused test covering the preserved dbca AC3 path.\n- [ ] The implementation lands in the same Gerrit change as ce6b and references both tickets.\n\n## Testing\nRun the focused workflow/error taxonomy tests added or updated for this ticket with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q`, then run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`. After commit, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" rebar verify-commit-ticket HEAD` to verify ticket trailers."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788287223400169402,"uuid":"0289dfe0-4fe2-42a9-88d5-f577fe8a7795"}